e_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3147854-ielts_trainer_2_academic_listening_test_2_4.wav","question_groups":[{"id":"en-trainer-2-t2-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><p><strong>The Engineer Sarah Guppy, 1770-1852</strong></p><p><strong>Background</strong></p><ul><li>women were active in many areas of 19th-century British society, e.g. Jane Harrison was the first female <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>by the end of the century there were 140 female dentists and 212 <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>, as well as many musicians and actors</li></ul><p><strong>Sarah Guppy</strong></p><ul><li>was born in Birmingham and moved to Bristol with her husband</li><li>designed bridges that could survive <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>built <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of the Clifton Suspension Bridge</li><li>was a significant <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in the Clifton Suspension Bridge together with her husband</li><li>designed a ‘barnacle buster’ that allowed <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> to go faster</li><li>helped stop <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> near railway lines</li><li>built an amusing machine for making different parts of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> at the same time</li><li>designed an early type of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> equipment</li></ul><p><strong>Conclusions</strong></p><ul><li>other women worked as engineers, e.g. Ada Lovelace and Hertha Marks Ayrton</li><li>it was not until 1906 that a woman <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in engineering</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/ielts_trainer_2_academic_listening_test_2_4.wav"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-trainer-2-t2-l-q1","part_id":"en-trainer-2-t2-l-p1",